                                "sense_id": "d1041f80-4195-3d17-b6d4-fb339f0df7bf",
                                "text": "The train of symptoms which mark the typhoid variety of scarlatina generally begin to decline about the tenth or twelfth day, when the case often lapses into a condition similar to rheumatic fever, without its characteristic diaphoreses."
                            }
                        ]
